  "result": "`slugify` is implemented in `src/strings.js`, and `npm test` passes (12 tests: the 2 existing ones and 10 new ones).\n\nIt follows your rules:\n- It turns `đ`/`Đ` into `d` first, then strips the remaining diacritics.\n- It lowercases and turns each run of non-`a-z0-9` characters into one hyphen.\n- It trims leading and trailing hyphens, cuts to 50 characters, then trims any hyphen left at the cut.\n\nI added the tests to `test/strings.test.js`. They cover:\n- basic casing\n- Vietnamese and other Latin diacritics\n- `đ`/`Đ`\n- runs of punctuation\n- trimming\n- digits\n- input that leaves nothing, which gives an empty string\n- the 50-character cap, including a cut that lands on a hyphen\n\nInput that isn't a string is converted with `String()` first, so `slugify(null)` gives `'null'`. I didn't add a test for that.",
